(3105771, 434363, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>Photographically speaking, you did a very nice job capturing this image under what had to be tough lighting conditions.  My only comment regarding the technical aspects of this image is the out of focus nut on the right side of the photo.  I''ve never been a big fan of objects in the front plane of a photo being out of focus but that is a personal preference and I try not to lower a score for such things.  Besides, at 1/45 sec, ISO 1600, and F5.3 (Hand held I assume), you did an amazing job with the limited depth of focus you had.<br/> <br/>As for your score, I think the comments you received during the challenge sum it up pretty well.  People had a small problem associating this image with the movie.  I am really amazed that the score didn''t suffer more from the DNMC crowd than it did.  That probably was related to this being a member challenge and not an open challenge.  <br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, Photographically speaking, you did a very nice job capturing this image under what had to be tough lighting conditions.  My only comment regarding the technical aspects of this image is the out of focus nut on the right side of the photo.  I''ve never been a big fan of objects in the front plane of a photo being out of focus but that is a personal preference and I try not to lower a score for such things.  Besides, at 1/45 sec, ISO 1600, and F5.3 (Hand held I assume), you did an amazing job with the limited depth of focus you had. As for your score, I think the comments you received during the challenge sum it up pretty well.  People had a small problem associating this image with the movie.  I am really amazed that the score didn''t suffer more from the DNMC crowd than it did.  That probably was related to this being a member challenge and not an open challenge.   Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2006-12-11 07:09:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3105787, 433853, 3032, '<td valign="top">Russian paintings rock! :)</td>', 'Russian paintings rock! :)', '2006-12-11 07:24:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3105792, 434215, 23484, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a really nice finish. Very sharp and detailed.</td>', 'Congratulations on a really nice finish. Very sharp and detailed.', '2006-12-11 07:28:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3105797, 433798, 27482, '<td valign="top">Nice shot buddy, well composed and definately met the challenge head on wich is of course critical to do well in challenges here.  Main problem here would be the lighting, it´s not bad at all but a little too strong on the hand and chips.  A good tip would be to keep the lighting simple while you are figuring it out, the most natural lighting will come from above from maybe a 45 degree angle as that is how we usually see people lit, the sun and lightbulbs usually come from an above angle :)<br/> <br/>Keep it up!</td>', 'Nice shot buddy, well composed and definately met the challenge head on wich is of course critical to do well in challenges here.  Main problem here would be the lighting, it´s not bad at all but a little too strong on the hand and chips.  A good tip would be to keep the lighting simple while you are figuring it out, the most natural lighting will come from above from maybe a 45 degree angle as that is how we usually see people lit, the sun and lightbulbs usually come from an above angle :) Keep it up!', '2006-12-11 07:30:52.000000', NULL, 0),
